<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Illovo half year shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Illovo half year shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr,(cts)    41.7	  vs 33.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 14.5	  vs 11.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   68.72	 vs 53.74</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   92.25	 vs 75.36</p>
<p>    Tax			 23.53	 vs 21.62</p>
<p>    Net financing costs   12.12	 vs 15.30</p>
<p>    Turnover		  974.31	vs 830.58</p>
<p>Div payable July 9</p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Illovo Sugar Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     1.75 profit vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - The South African sugar company said it expected its growth rate for headline earnings per share for the year to be similar to that seen in the first half.</p>
<p>The firm also added that it was continuing to evaluate new investments in the rest of Africa such as Lonrho Sugar and the privatisation of the Kenyan and Ivory Coast sugar industries.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
